Only after these reports are approved should any code changes begin.Rather than giving this as a single prompt, break the work into phases. Ask the AI IDE to complete the Architecture Audit first and review its output before asking it to generate the schema or modify code. Then proceed to the migration plan, and only after you've reviewed both should you let it implement changes. This review gate catches incorrect assumptions early and greatly reduces the chance of a large, hard-to-debug rewrite.